WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.449 --> 00:00:03.659
Well, actually, I’ve always been interested
in bees.

00:00:03.659 --> 00:00:08.890
They’re the pinnacle of social evolution,
really, in the whole animal kingdom.

00:00:08.890 --> 00:00:15.490
But my interest in their gut bacteria in particular
developed when there was a study right after

00:00:15.490 --> 00:00:19.750
the first colony collapse event which was
2007.

00:00:19.750 --> 00:00:24.190
There was a study of the organisms associated
with bees in attempt to find what disease

00:00:24.190 --> 00:00:26.140
organism might be involved.

00:00:26.140 --> 00:00:30.251
And one thing that came out of that — it
didn’t identify a disease organism, but

00:00:30.251 --> 00:00:35.720
it did show that there was a set number of
bacteria that live in every single honeybee

00:00:35.720 --> 00:00:39.620
everywhere in the world and that these are
dominating the gut of those bees.

00:00:39.620 --> 00:00:44.640
And that made me think this is a good system
for really looking at a very specialized community

00:00:44.640 --> 00:00:48.020
that’s probably doing something important
in bees.

